<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue `kuna-indirectonly` (P6, sub-stage merge-aggressiveness).

    An ILLEGAL INPUT is an input Varnode that ActionDirectWrite never reached,
    so nothing a formal parameter feeds can be responsible for its value: on a
    normal frame, the leftover contents of a stack slot the function overwrites
    before it reads.  Merge::mergeTestAdjacent refuses every speculative merge
    involving such a variable, and HighVariable::hasName refuses to name an
    unaffected input whose members are all of that kind.  Both refusals end
    "unless the illegal input is only used indirectly", and that exception needs
    the `indirectonly` Varnode flag, which nothing in kuna set:
    Funcdata::markIndirectOnly / checkIndirectUse (funcdata_varnode.cc:801-858)
    were unported and ActionMarkIndirectOnly was a documented no-op, so
    isIndirectOnly() answered false everywhere.

    Synthetic minimiser, the shape coreutils `date` -O0 `main` has (gcc frame,
    the `struct timespec when` at -0xc0(%rbp) whose address escapes on the other
    branch, filled from one call result by a divide and a remainder):

      take:  push rbp / mov rbp,rsp / sub rsp,0x120
             mov eax,[c1] / test eax,eax / je 102d
             lea rax,[rbp-0xc0] / mov rdi,rax / mov rsi,[str] / call parse
             jmp 106c
      102d:  call now_ns                      ; the value, in RAX
             mov [rbp-0xc8],rax               ; a temp
             mov rdi,1000000000
             mov rcx,[rbp-0xc8] / mov rax,rcx / cqo / idiv rdi
             mov [rbp-0xc0],rax               ; when.tv_sec  = v / 1e9
             mov rcx,[rbp-0xc8] / mov rax,rcx / cqo / idiv rdi
             mov [rbp-0xb8],rdx               ; when.tv_nsec = v % 1e9
      106c:  lea rax,[rbp-0xc0] / mov rdi,rax / call use / leave / ret

    `lea rbp-0xc0` escapes the struct, so both of its slots are address-tied and
    the value each holds on entry reaches nothing but the INDIRECTs of the calls
   , indirect-only.  The COPY that writes the remainder into `when.tv_nsec`
    wants to merge RAX's HighVariable, which also carries the call's result,
    into that slot.

    Pass 1 (option indirectonly off): the merge is refused, the call result gets
    its own register local, and the slot is assigned across -> #1, #2.
    Pass 2 (option indirectonly on, the default): the merge happens, the call
    result is computed straight into `when.tv_nsec`, and the register local is
    gone -> #3, #4, #5.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="take"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x107d" name="parse"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1081" name="now_ns"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1087" name="use"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option indirectonly off</com>
  <com>lo fu take</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option indirectonly on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #1: off spills the call result to its own register local" min="1" max="1">v1 = now_ns\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #2: off assigns the remainder across into the escaped slot" min="1" max="1">v3 = v1 % 1000000000;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #3: on computes the call result straight into the slot" min="1" max="1">v2 = now_ns\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #4: on folds the remainder back into that same slot" min="1" max="1">v2 %= 1000000000;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="indirectonly #5: the register temp is declared only in pass 1 (one local fewer on)" min="1" max="1">int8 v1; // rax</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
